 <bp:standardName rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Choline kinase alpha</bp:standardName>
 <bp:xref rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/UnificationXref_uniprot_knowledgebase_P35790" />
 <bp:xref rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/RelationshipXref_hgnc_symbol_CHKA_identity" />
 <bp:organism rdf:resource="http://identifiers.org/taxonomy/9606" />
 <bp:displayName rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">CHKA_HUMAN</bp:displayName>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">CKI</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">CHKA</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">CHETK-alpha</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">EK</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">CHK</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">CK</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2.7.1.82</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2.7.1.32</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Ethanolamine kinase</bp:name>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">CHKA_HUMAN Reviewed; 457 AA.</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">FUNCTION: Has a key role in phospholipid biosynthesis and maycontribute to tumor cell growth. Catalyzes the first step inphosphatidylcholine biosynthesis. Contributes tophosphatidylethanolamine biosynthesis. Phosphorylates choline andethanolamine. Has higher activity with choline.{ECO:0000269|PubMed:19915674}.CATALYTIC ACTIVITY:Reaction=ATP + choline = ADP + H(+) + phosphocholine;Xref=Rhea:RHEA:12837, ChEBI:CHEBI:15354, ChEBI:CHEBI:15378,ChEBI:CHEBI:30616, ChEBI:CHEBI:295975, ChEBI:CHEBI:456216;EC=2.7.1.32; Evidence={ECO:0000269|PubMed:19915674};PhysiologicalDirection=left-to-right; Xref=Rhea:RHEA:12838;Evidence={ECO:0000305|PubMed:19915674};CATALYTIC ACTIVITY:Reaction=ATP + ethanolamine = ADP + H(+) + phosphoethanolamine;Xref=Rhea:RHEA:13069, ChEBI:CHEBI:15378, ChEBI:CHEBI:30616,ChEBI:CHEBI:57603, ChEBI:CHEBI:58190, ChEBI:CHEBI:456216;EC=2.7.1.82; Evidence={ECO:0000269|PubMed:19915674};PhysiologicalDirection=left-to-right; Xref=Rhea:RHEA:13070;Evidence={ECO:0000305|PubMed:19915674};BIOPHYSICOCHEMICAL PROPERTIES:Kinetic parameters:KM=0.2 mM for choline {ECO:0000269|PubMed:17007874,ECO:0000269|PubMed:19915674};KM=0.4 mM for ATP {ECO:0000269|PubMed:17007874,ECO:0000269|PubMed:19915674};KM=12 mM for ethanolamine {ECO:0000269|PubMed:17007874,ECO:0000269|PubMed:19915674};PATHWAY: Phospholipid metabolism; phosphatidylcholinebiosynthesis; phosphocholine from choline: step 1/1.{ECO:0000305|PubMed:17007874, ECO:0000305|PubMed:19915674}.PATHWAY: Phospholipid metabolism; phosphatidylethanolaminebiosynthesis; phosphatidylethanolamine from ethanolamine: step1/3. {ECO:0000305|PubMed:17007874, ECO:0000305|PubMed:19915674}.SUBUNIT: Heterodimer with CHKB (By similarity). Homodimer.{ECO:0000250, ECO:0000269|PubMed:17007874,ECO:0000269|PubMed:20299452}.SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Cytoplasm.ALTERNATIVE PRODUCTS:Event=Alternative splicing; Named isoforms=2;Name=1;IsoId=P35790-1; Sequence=Displayed;Name=2;IsoId=P35790-2; Sequence=VSP_009683;SIMILARITY: Belongs to the choline/ethanolamine kinase family.{ECO:0000305}.WEB RESOURCE: Name=Atlas of Genetics and Cytogenetics in Oncologyand Haematology;URL=&quot;http://atlasgeneticsoncology.org/Genes/CHKAID44009ch11q13.html&quot;; COPYRIGHT: UniProt Consortium (www.uniprot.org). Distributed under the Creative Commons Attribution-NoDerivs License.</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://www.ctdbase.org/#ref_protein_gene_1119</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://www.phosphosite.org/phosphosite.owl#po_1288990</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://biocyc.org/biopax/biopax-level3ProteinReference113818</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/ProteinReference_uniprotkb_P35790_identity</bp:comment>
</bp:ProteinReference>

