<bp:ProteinReference rdf:about="http://identifiers.org/uniprot/Q8TCT1">
 <bp:entityFeature rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/ModificationFeature_285638da7fbd14b030bb9dc13c5f660b" />
 <bp:entityFeature rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/ModificationFeature_a6917706420bfb0a2d0284521cfc3f69" />
 <bp:standardName rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Phosphoethanolamine/phosphocholine phosphatase</bp:standardName>
 <bp:xref rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/UnificationXref_uniprot_knowledgebase_Q8TCT1" />
 <bp:xref rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/RelationshipXref_hgnc_symbol_PHOSPHO1_identity" />
 <bp:organism rdf:resource="http://identifiers.org/taxonomy/9606" />
 <bp:displayName rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">PHOP1_HUMAN</bp:displayName>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">PHOSPHO1</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">3.1.3.75</bp:name>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">PHOP1_HUMAN Reviewed; 267 AA.</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://mirtarbase.mbc.nctu.edu.tw/#ref_162466</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">FUNCTION: Phosphatase that has a high activity towardphosphoethanolamine (PEA) and phosphocholine (PCho). Involved inthe generation of inorganic phosphate for bone mineralization.CATALYTIC ACTIVITY:Reaction=H2O + phosphoethanolamine = ethanolamine + phosphate;Xref=Rhea:RHEA:16089, ChEBI:CHEBI:15377, ChEBI:CHEBI:43474,ChEBI:CHEBI:57603, ChEBI:CHEBI:58190; EC=3.1.3.75;Evidence={ECO:0000269|PubMed:15175005};CATALYTIC ACTIVITY:Reaction=H2O + phosphocholine = choline + phosphate;Xref=Rhea:RHEA:10492, ChEBI:CHEBI:15354, ChEBI:CHEBI:15377,ChEBI:CHEBI:43474, ChEBI:CHEBI:295975; EC=3.1.3.75;Evidence={ECO:0000269|PubMed:15175005};COFACTOR:Name=Mg(2+); Xref=ChEBI:CHEBI:18420;Evidence={ECO:0000269|PubMed:15175005};BIOPHYSICOCHEMICAL PROPERTIES:Kinetic parameters:KM=3 uM for PEA {ECO:0000269|PubMed:15175005};KM=11.4 uM for PCho {ECO:0000269|PubMed:15175005};pH dependence:Optimum pH is 6.7. {ECO:0000269|PubMed:15175005};ALTERNATIVE PRODUCTS:Event=Alternative splicing; Named isoforms=3;Name=1;IsoId=Q8TCT1-1; Sequence=Displayed;Name=2; Synonyms=PHOSPHO1-3a;IsoId=Q8TCT1-2; Sequence=VSP_040624;Name=3;IsoId=Q8TCT1-3; Sequence=VSP_045709;Note=No experimental confirmation available.;TISSUE SPECIFICITY: Expressed at sites of mineralization in boneand cartilage. Highly expressed in osteoblast cell line SaOS-2which produces a mineralized matrix, but not in MG-63 cell line,which do not mineralize. {ECO:0000269|PubMed:15050893}.SIMILARITY: Belongs to the HAD-like hydrolase superfamily. PHOSPHOfamily. {ECO:0000305}. COPYRIGHT: UniProt Consortium (www.uniprot.org). Distributed under the Creative Commons Attribution-NoDerivs License.</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://biocyc.org/biopax/biopax-level3ProteinReference90389</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://identifiers.org/uniprot.isoform/Q8TCT1-2</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/ProteinReference_uniprotkb_Q8TCT1_identity</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://identifiers.org/refseq/XP_005257166</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://www.ctdbase.org/#ref_protein_gene_162466</bp:comment>
</bp:ProteinReference>

