 <bp:standardName rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">3-ketoacyl-CoA thiolase, mitochondrial</bp:standardName>
 <bp:xref rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/RelationshipXref_hgnc_symbol_ACAA2_identity" />
 <bp:xref rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/UnificationXref_uniprot_knowledgebase_P42765" />
 <bp:organism rdf:resource="http://identifiers.org/taxonomy/9606" />
 <bp:displayName rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">THIM_HUMAN</bp:displayName>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">ACAA2</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2.3.1.16</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Acyl-CoA hydrolase, mitochondrial</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Mitochondrial 3-oxoacyl-CoA thiolase</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Acetyl-CoA acetyltransferase</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">3.1.2.1</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">3.1.2.2</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Acetyl-CoA acyltransferase</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Beta-ketothiolase</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">3.1.2.-</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">T1</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2.3.1.9</bp:name>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">FUNCTION: In the production of energy from fats, this is one ofthe enzymes that catalyzes the last step of the mitochondrialbeta-oxidation pathway, an aerobic process breaking down fattyacids into acetyl-CoA (Probable). Using free coenzyme A/CoA,catalyzes the thiolytic cleavage of medium- to long-chainunbranched 3-oxoacyl-CoAs into acetyl-CoA and a fatty acyl-CoAshortened by two carbon atoms (Probable). Also catalyzes thecondensation of two acetyl-CoA molecules into acetoacetyl-CoA andcould be involved in the production of ketone bodies (Probable).Also displays hydrolase activity on various fatty acyl-CoAs(PubMed:25478839). Thereby, could be responsible for theproduction of acetate in a side reaction to beta-oxidation(Probable). Abolishes BNIP3-mediated apoptosis and mitochondrialdamage (PubMed:18371312). {ECO:0000269|PubMed:18371312,ECO:0000269|PubMed:25478839, ECO:0000305|PubMed:25478839}.CATALYTIC ACTIVITY:Reaction=acetyl-CoA + an acyl-CoA = a 3-oxoacyl-CoA + CoA;Xref=Rhea:RHEA:21564, ChEBI:CHEBI:57287, ChEBI:CHEBI:57288,ChEBI:CHEBI:58342, ChEBI:CHEBI:90726; EC=2.3.1.16;Evidence={ECO:0000269|PubMed:25478839};PhysiologicalDirection=left-to-right; Xref=Rhea:RHEA:21565;Evidence={ECO:0000305|PubMed:25478839};PhysiologicalDirection=right-to-left; Xref=Rhea:RHEA:21566;Evidence={ECO:0000305|PubMed:25478839};CATALYTIC ACTIVITY:Reaction=2 acetyl-CoA = acetoacetyl-CoA + CoA;Xref=Rhea:RHEA:21036, ChEBI:CHEBI:57286, ChEBI:CHEBI:57287,ChEBI:CHEBI:57288; EC=2.3.1.9;Evidence={ECO:0000269|PubMed:25478839};PhysiologicalDirection=left-to-right; Xref=Rhea:RHEA:21037;Evidence={ECO:0000305|PubMed:25478839};PhysiologicalDirection=right-to-left; Xref=Rhea:RHEA:21038;Evidence={ECO:0000305|PubMed:25478839};CATALYTIC ACTIVITY:Reaction=acetyl-CoA + H2O = acetate + CoA + H(+);Xref=Rhea:RHEA:20289, ChEBI:CHEBI:15377, ChEBI:CHEBI:15378,ChEBI:CHEBI:30089, ChEBI:CHEBI:57287, ChEBI:CHEBI:57288;EC=3.1.2.1; Evidence={ECO:0000269|PubMed:25478839};PhysiologicalDirection=left-to-right; Xref=Rhea:RHEA:20290;Evidence={ECO:0000305|PubMed:25478839};CATALYTIC ACTIVITY:Reaction=H2O + propanoyl-CoA = CoA + H(+) + propanoate;Xref=Rhea:RHEA:40103, ChEBI:CHEBI:15377, ChEBI:CHEBI:15378,ChEBI:CHEBI:17272, ChEBI:CHEBI:57287, ChEBI:CHEBI:57392;Evidence={ECO:0000269|PubMed:25478839};PhysiologicalDirection=left-to-right; Xref=Rhea:RHEA:40104;Evidence={ECO:0000305|PubMed:25478839};CATALYTIC ACTIVITY:Reaction=butanoyl-CoA + H2O = butanoate + CoA + H(+);Xref=Rhea:RHEA:40111, ChEBI:CHEBI:15377, ChEBI:CHEBI:15378,ChEBI:CHEBI:17968, ChEBI:CHEBI:57287, ChEBI:CHEBI:57371;Evidence={ECO:0000269|PubMed:25478839};PhysiologicalDirection=left-to-right; Xref=Rhea:RHEA:40112;Evidence={ECO:0000305|PubMed:25478839};CATALYTIC ACTIVITY:Reaction=H2O + hexanoyl-CoA = CoA + H(+) + hexanoate;Xref=Rhea:RHEA:40115, ChEBI:CHEBI:15377, ChEBI:CHEBI:15378,ChEBI:CHEBI:17120, ChEBI:CHEBI:57287, ChEBI:CHEBI:62620;Evidence={ECO:0000269|PubMed:25478839};PhysiologicalDirection=left-to-right; Xref=Rhea:RHEA:40116;Evidence={ECO:0000305|PubMed:25478839};CATALYTIC ACTIVITY:Reaction=H2O + octanoyl-CoA = CoA + H(+) + octanoate;Xref=Rhea:RHEA:30143, ChEBI:CHEBI:15377, ChEBI:CHEBI:15378,ChEBI:CHEBI:25646, ChEBI:CHEBI:57287, ChEBI:CHEBI:57386;Evidence={ECO:0000269|PubMed:25478839};PhysiologicalDirection=left-to-right; Xref=Rhea:RHEA:30144;Evidence={ECO:0000305|PubMed:25478839};CATALYTIC ACTIVITY:Reaction=decanoyl-CoA + H2O = CoA + decanoate + H(+);Xref=Rhea:RHEA:40059, ChEBI:CHEBI:15377, ChEBI:CHEBI:15378,ChEBI:CHEBI:27689, ChEBI:CHEBI:57287, ChEBI:CHEBI:61430;Evidence={ECO:0000269|PubMed:25478839};PhysiologicalDirection=left-to-right; Xref=Rhea:RHEA:40060;Evidence={ECO:0000305|PubMed:25478839};CATALYTIC ACTIVITY:Reaction=dodecanoyl-CoA + H2O = CoA + dodecanoate + H(+);Xref=Rhea:RHEA:30135, ChEBI:CHEBI:15377, ChEBI:CHEBI:15378,ChEBI:CHEBI:18262, ChEBI:CHEBI:57287, ChEBI:CHEBI:57375;Evidence={ECO:0000269|PubMed:25478839};PhysiologicalDirection=left-to-right; Xref=Rhea:RHEA:30136;Evidence={ECO:0000305|PubMed:25478839};CATALYTIC ACTIVITY:Reaction=H2O + tetradecanoyl-CoA = CoA + H(+) + tetradecanoate;Xref=Rhea:RHEA:40119, ChEBI:CHEBI:15377, ChEBI:CHEBI:15378,ChEBI:CHEBI:30807, ChEBI:CHEBI:57287, ChEBI:CHEBI:57385;Evidence={ECO:0000269|PubMed:25478839};PhysiologicalDirection=left-to-right; Xref=Rhea:RHEA:40120;Evidence={ECO:0000305|PubMed:25478839};CATALYTIC ACTIVITY:Reaction=H2O + hexadecanoyl-CoA = CoA + H(+) + hexadecanoate;Xref=Rhea:RHEA:16645, ChEBI:CHEBI:7896, ChEBI:CHEBI:15377,ChEBI:CHEBI:15378, ChEBI:CHEBI:57287, ChEBI:CHEBI:57379;EC=3.1.2.2; Evidence={ECO:0000250|UniProtKB:P13437};PhysiologicalDirection=left-to-right; Xref=Rhea:RHEA:16646;Evidence={ECO:0000250|UniProtKB:P13437};BIOPHYSICOCHEMICAL PROPERTIES:Kinetic parameters:KM=9.2 uM for acetoacetyl-CoA {ECO:0000269|PubMed:25478839};KM=250 uM for acetyl-CoA {ECO:0000269|PubMed:25478839};KM=35 uM for octanoyl-CoA {ECO:0000269|PubMed:25478839};Note=kcat is 14.8 sec(-1) for the degradation of acetoacetyl-CoA(3-oxoacyl-CoA thiolase) (PubMed:25478839). kcat is 1.4 sec(-1)for the synthesis of acetoacetyl-CoA (PubMed:25478839). kcat is0.02 sec(-1) for octanoyl-CoA hydrolysis (PubMed:25478839).{ECO:0000269|PubMed:25478839};PATHWAY: Lipid metabolism; fatty acid beta-oxidation.{ECO:0000269|PubMed:25478839}.SUBUNIT: Homotetramer (PubMed:25478839). Interacts with BNIP3.{ECO:0000269|PubMed:18371312, ECO:0000269|PubMed:25478839}.SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Mitochondrion {ECO:0000269|PubMed:18371312}.SIMILARITY: Belongs to the thiolase-like superfamily. Thiolasefamily. {ECO:0000305}. COPYRIGHT: UniProt Consortium (www.uniprot.org). Distributed under the Creative Commons Attribution-NoDerivs License.</bp:comment>
