 <bp:standardName rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Fructose-bisphosphate aldolase C</bp:standardName>
 <bp:xref rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/UnificationXref_uniprot_knowledgebase_P09972" />
 <bp:xref rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/RelationshipXref_hgnc_symbol_ALDOC_identity" />
 <bp:organism rdf:resource="http://identifiers.org/taxonomy/9606" />
 <bp:displayName rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">ALDOC_HUMAN</bp:displayName>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">ALDC</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Brain-type aldolase</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">ALDOC</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">4.1.2.13</bp:name>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://mirtarbase.mbc.nctu.edu.tw/#ref_230</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://www.ctdbase.org/#ref_protein_gene_230</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">ALDOC_HUMAN Reviewed; 364 AA.</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/ProteinReference_HPRD_02386_identity</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">CATALYTIC ACTIVITY:Reaction=beta-D-fructose 1,6-bisphosphate = D-glyceraldehyde 3-phosphate + dihydroxyacetone phosphate; Xref=Rhea:RHEA:14729,ChEBI:CHEBI:32966, ChEBI:CHEBI:57642, ChEBI:CHEBI:59776;EC=4.1.2.13; Evidence={ECO:0000269|PubMed:15537755};BIOPHYSICOCHEMICAL PROPERTIES:Kinetic parameters:KM=10.7 uM for fructose 1,6-bisphosphate{ECO:0000269|PubMed:15537755};KM=16 mM for fructose 1-phosphate {ECO:0000269|PubMed:15537755};PATHWAY: Carbohydrate degradation; glycolysis; D-glyceraldehyde 3-phosphate and glycerone phosphate from D-glucose: step 4/4.SUBUNIT: Homotetramer. Interacts with ATP6V1E1. May interact withPLD2. {ECO:0000269|PubMed:11399750, ECO:0000269|PubMed:11876650}.MISCELLANEOUS: In vertebrates, three forms of this ubiquitousglycolytic enzyme are found, aldolase A in muscle, aldolase B inliver and aldolase C in brain.SIMILARITY: Belongs to the class I fructose-bisphosphate aldolasefamily. {ECO:0000305}.SEQUENCE CAUTION:Sequence=AAI03761.1; Type=Erroneous initiation; Evidence={ECO:0000305}; COPYRIGHT: UniProt Consortium (www.uniprot.org). Distributed under the Creative Commons Attribution-NoDerivs License.</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/ProteinReference_uniprotkb_P09972_identity</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://identifiers.org/refseq/NP_005156</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/ProteinReference_rcsb_pdb_1XFB_see-also</bp:comment>
</bp:ProteinReference>

